[{:db/id "q-105792/selection/427eed9745f9826771c272c26d43848dd7bfa2b39f56f72bd07ecc094ab1d5a9" :answer/id #uuid "ced3deef-3369-5c92-a6fd-58af86179357" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,i+j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105792/selection/67823992b9e86d4b18f53ff99b67228121b8691bd33db0ca84d8dad193a44251" :answer/id #uuid "13f27617-a400-5fd7-b620-5fa97930df42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j+2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105792/selection/c960b96291e3d6d275c2ac8bbc9b9425a4794afd8f2b12a3ae0268df62999a9e" :answer/id #uuid "e68e5919-ec7e-5c94-a7bd-0338054e031b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105792/selection/97610aa569b7313cc3a16ef97679c510c11ec2515cbf1a251c586711c95b7093" :answer/id #uuid "700756f4-8079-5c3a-954a-c8f8d7280d2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105792/selection/f19886ee7578539144f73f3aedc7157f16b923f0f0dd37e59452a6e1d2c426c3" :answer/id #uuid "8819badf-2126-561b-b89a-c0fe25315da4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105792/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9001483-ab22-5284-bda2-cad4963b5d32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105792/selection/f19886ee7578539144f73f3aedc7157f16b923f0f0dd37e59452a6e1d2c426c3" :answer-field/choices ["q-105792/selection/427eed9745f9826771c272c26d43848dd7bfa2b39f56f72bd07ecc094ab1d5a9" "q-105792/selection/67823992b9e86d4b18f53ff99b67228121b8691bd33db0ca84d8dad193a44251" "q-105792/selection/c960b96291e3d6d275c2ac8bbc9b9425a4794afd8f2b12a3ae0268df62999a9e" "q-105792/selection/97610aa569b7313cc3a16ef97679c510c11ec2515cbf1a251c586711c95b7093" "q-105792/selection/f19886ee7578539144f73f3aedc7157f16b923f0f0dd37e59452a6e1d2c426c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105792" :question/id #uuid "a1665578-dbd9-50ec-867b-48ff886a6d85" :question/math-academy-id "q-105792" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (2F-G)$ at the point $(0,-1,2)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={e}^{x}\\,i+yz\\,j,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=z\\,i+(x+2y)\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F-G) & =∇\\times (2F)+∇\\times (-G) \\\\  & =2∇\\times F-∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {e}^{x} & yz & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(yz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{x})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x})]k \\\\  & =(0-y)i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-y\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F-G) & =2∇\\times F-∇\\times G \\\\  & =2[-y\\,i]-[z\\,i+(x+2y)\\,k] \\\\  & =-2y\\,i-z\\,i-(x+2y)\\,k \\\\  & =-(2y+z)\\,i-(x+2y)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,-1,2),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (2F-G))(0,-1,2) & =-(2(-1)+2)\\,i-(0+2(-1))\\,k \\\\  & =-(-2+2)\\,i-(0-2)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105792/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105792"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131438/selection/3b288e9941b391ffd3104d1a7a4974801c505d76e45bdfa0bd8c03d5b7acef6f" :answer/id #uuid "bd401888-cbb5-5a88-87bf-0bad8266a1df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\,i+2\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131438/selection/242d2942780431714996b99a6c10467fd0792ceef6fdb43584ff12698a5952cd" :answer/id #uuid "9f7b4ca3-f0f8-5a03-a395-34da262f0036" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\,j+2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131438/selection/7287b3213021430704a2fb29e7c4f68aead8a74740056ee0f43339465e6e23f5" :answer/id #uuid "61088d69-1d7a-5f6e-8c07-ecd6a1fa14a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,j+\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131438/selection/28b79870f8853519776c0f40363317339896ee1bdfd989865ddc5981fad46223" :answer/id #uuid "18b62c7e-d6f9-51bd-92c8-7dc6f5e35f2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\,i+3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131438/selection/f946981d2c5be317f9f17be9387ffdd763d0f0c73a5db77639e15bc4f994c9ca" :answer/id #uuid "0059eb54-75a2-552e-8917-d49d8f2bbfde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,j+3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131438/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c7f9950-13d6-5ba6-8b2d-22942eb199b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131438/selection/242d2942780431714996b99a6c10467fd0792ceef6fdb43584ff12698a5952cd" :answer-field/choices ["q-131438/selection/3b288e9941b391ffd3104d1a7a4974801c505d76e45bdfa0bd8c03d5b7acef6f" "q-131438/selection/242d2942780431714996b99a6c10467fd0792ceef6fdb43584ff12698a5952cd" "q-131438/selection/7287b3213021430704a2fb29e7c4f68aead8a74740056ee0f43339465e6e23f5" "q-131438/selection/28b79870f8853519776c0f40363317339896ee1bdfd989865ddc5981fad46223" "q-131438/selection/f946981d2c5be317f9f17be9387ffdd763d0f0c73a5db77639e15bc4f994c9ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131438" :question/id #uuid "1fdcb434-8b1a-5fda-8318-f1384fd1027b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131438" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (F+G)$ at the point $(0,1,2)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z\\,i+xz\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{z}^{2}\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {x}^{2}z & xz & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}z)]k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x)i-(0-{x}^{2})j+(z-0)k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x)\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j+z\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-x)\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j+z\\,k+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{z}^{2}\\,j-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,k \\\\  & =-x\\,i+({x}^{2}-{z}^{2})\\,j+(z-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,2),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (F+G))(0,1,2)=-4\\,j+2\\,k.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131438/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131438"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105799/selection/bbd0d8496212cc4d13ce50b6b4a208543163fc14693461fa683ab36ce15d08ef" :answer/id #uuid "ccd9a539-fa59-5703-8ef2-8f2cf99adc88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105799/selection/73b2730709cec47036ca305057bb93c966ffbd8010212d813976103822feaf3b" :answer/id #uuid "c3636553-1423-5df2-8b08-0dbf6102ad57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i-j+2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105799/selection/080453a63d7b02e0a9496f1473afe74b7a50e734b309842138d5c0d2c3aa47c4" :answer/id #uuid "c52fdaa0-8514-5cb4-8982-68237f8a528a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-i-5\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105799/selection/33e783c31e3fd72f022c0a01a30232cd8d147828f9b2d13ea5504aaf9c27784a" :answer/id #uuid "5a9ac62a-182d-59c7-bdc9-059350e68a51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,i+j-3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105799/selection/d264dc02215fd412512123cf3d17dc3a811ebbc248d44942d86e12594675f9e6" :answer/id #uuid "4492f0b6-5a12-5841-b40d-0cd8459518f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "j-2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105799/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "65f957cb-d9e6-555c-9f05-3d646c84456b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105799/selection/080453a63d7b02e0a9496f1473afe74b7a50e734b309842138d5c0d2c3aa47c4" :answer-field/choices ["q-105799/selection/bbd0d8496212cc4d13ce50b6b4a208543163fc14693461fa683ab36ce15d08ef" "q-105799/selection/73b2730709cec47036ca305057bb93c966ffbd8010212d813976103822feaf3b" "q-105799/selection/080453a63d7b02e0a9496f1473afe74b7a50e734b309842138d5c0d2c3aa47c4" "q-105799/selection/33e783c31e3fd72f022c0a01a30232cd8d147828f9b2d13ea5504aaf9c27784a" "q-105799/selection/d264dc02215fd412512123cf3d17dc3a811ebbc248d44942d86e12594675f9e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105799" :question/id #uuid "39f7b901-580a-5a32-ab40-fb1a6dc62a95" :question/math-academy-id "q-105799" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (F+3G)$ at the point $(0,1,-2)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={y}^{2}\\,i+z\\,j+{x}^{2}\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=-3{x}^{2}\\,j-k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+3G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times (3G) \\\\  & =∇\\times F+3∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {y}^{2} & z & {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(0-1)i-(2x-0)j+(0-2y)k \\\\  & =-i-2x\\,j-2y\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+3G) & =∇\\times F+3∇\\times G \\\\  & =-i-2x\\,j-2y\\,k+3[-3{x}^{2}\\,j-k] \\\\  & =-i-2x\\,j-2y\\,k-9{x}^{2}\\,j-3k \\\\  & =-i-(9{x}^{2}+2x)\\,j-(2y+3)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,-2),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F+3G))(0,1,-2) & =-i-(9(0)^{2}+2(0))\\,j-(2(1)+3)\\,k \\\\  & =-i-5\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105799/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105799"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131434/selection/7381a3cd60f3a5547f59671910587f9b52d2d9ad7df557429bb95c44eec2a71f" :answer/id #uuid "3a54f2ac-9e06-504c-b34a-6394c7055245" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,j+2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131434/selection/7fc44339767192def569051958b4da8a6320146f6867510d397160a8bafc7f59" :answer/id #uuid "5427f56d-2cc6-5a46-8355-4c85a2e7ea48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,i-2\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131434/selection/e6687804528e1c24811b782e25304c57198417e7c8aa659f5908a36e08482056" :answer/id #uuid "14823473-80e8-5ec4-9d5b-a6bdf8bdbc25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\,j+5\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131434/selection/d130a431e0ba9cbc8927398522f852a8a872ee210adea1b63d6f8daf427b4fe3" :answer/id #uuid "6bfaae6e-2805-56d8-9ad3-37ce63990e40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,i+3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131434/selection/1775c8e1c3ae6b1a2c8287980600b925cb1d7a8edb7d8d09cd111d41f7567960" :answer/id #uuid "e20dadf9-6b55-5856-b68e-2fe632b2e438" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\,i+5\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131434/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "130a2b65-9915-5cb5-ab83-d408d5b2d5aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131434/selection/e6687804528e1c24811b782e25304c57198417e7c8aa659f5908a36e08482056" :answer-field/choices ["q-131434/selection/7381a3cd60f3a5547f59671910587f9b52d2d9ad7df557429bb95c44eec2a71f" "q-131434/selection/7fc44339767192def569051958b4da8a6320146f6867510d397160a8bafc7f59" "q-131434/selection/e6687804528e1c24811b782e25304c57198417e7c8aa659f5908a36e08482056" "q-131434/selection/d130a431e0ba9cbc8927398522f852a8a872ee210adea1b63d6f8daf427b4fe3" "q-131434/selection/1775c8e1c3ae6b1a2c8287980600b925cb1d7a8edb7d8d09cd111d41f7567960"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131434" :question/id #uuid "5669465a-097d-533e-a021-36c62b5eb0bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-131434" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (2F+G)$ at the point $(-1,2,0)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=xyz\\,i+xy\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=xy\\,j-x\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F+G) & =∇\\times (2F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =2∇\\times F+∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ xyz & xy & {z}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xyz)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz)]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-xy)j+(y-xz)k \\\\  & =xy\\,j+(y-xz)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F+G) & =2∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =2[xy\\,j+(y-xz)\\,k]+xy\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =2xy\\,j+2(y-xz)\\,k+xy\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =3xy\\,j+(2y-2xz-x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,2,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (2F+G))(-1,2,0)=-6\\,j+5\\,k.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131434/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131434"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131437/selection/fe0734cd852f7ba962727013a53c235b063a3c50a04d2a62f8ae950e35819fc1" :answer/id #uuid "a343b05d-7140-533d-8d3c-12ae58f91e92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,i-2k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131437/selection/ae6ce28635f6585cd1a77fd4ad3f2e09d8b6c15282277c8f00219a34951cb576" :answer/id #uuid "c0a40303-daac-54ca-818d-bd9dee24783d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131437/selection/e97042e68f37bc20bd196146ef278a42ebcdf500de60cb5381ca680da36a878e" :answer/id #uuid "7fa26c49-f759-54e8-8437-fe77b7aaeea7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131437/selection/a1c1ed8a6a4283ee5d48bfbe772eb402594811d663bc5cc20319586ce61aa8f0" :answer/id #uuid "6c91d2ef-3889-544c-9a6f-9ea4c81cc927" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,i+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131437/selection/fed16e41dd940dad149a1900292d74d79d3c1038c29b56d78dca3fa8ed492f95" :answer/id #uuid "55975849-7efa-5814-86e7-af8390c9f36f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,i+3j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131437/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e6ac360-523f-573f-a058-853ddd399e44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131437/selection/a1c1ed8a6a4283ee5d48bfbe772eb402594811d663bc5cc20319586ce61aa8f0" :answer-field/choices ["q-131437/selection/fe0734cd852f7ba962727013a53c235b063a3c50a04d2a62f8ae950e35819fc1" "q-131437/selection/ae6ce28635f6585cd1a77fd4ad3f2e09d8b6c15282277c8f00219a34951cb576" "q-131437/selection/e97042e68f37bc20bd196146ef278a42ebcdf500de60cb5381ca680da36a878e" "q-131437/selection/a1c1ed8a6a4283ee5d48bfbe772eb402594811d663bc5cc20319586ce61aa8f0" "q-131437/selection/fed16e41dd940dad149a1900292d74d79d3c1038c29b56d78dca3fa8ed492f95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131437" :question/id #uuid "09bed0fa-1349-51db-829d-2a5d714d05fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-131437" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (F-2G)$ at the point $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2},-1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=xy\\,i+xz\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i-x\\,k.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-2G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times (2G) \\\\  & =∇\\times F-2∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ xy & xz & \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)]k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-x)i-(0-0)j+(z-x)k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-x)\\,i+(z-x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-2G) & =∇\\times F-2∇\\times G \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-x)\\,i+(z-x)\\,k-2[-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i-x\\,k] \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-x)\\,i+(z-x)\\,k+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+2x\\,k \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-x)\\,i+(z+x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2},-1),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (F-2G))(2,\\frac{\\pi }{2},-1)=-\\,i+k.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131437/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131437"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105962/selection/eee5a3a8e12930dd100249b1242ad7e1794b48a6f0e204e718f698c7792ed534" :answer/id #uuid "8fc4f752-33a4-5aa4-9e83-487873b493af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,0,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105962/selection/613f439dc6324c3c1f9ff32eea8f2121282ac7a544cf9d808b85c34a9e6b0b25" :answer/id #uuid "7e99c295-5956-5d0b-baea-ba3242be9bf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-4,0,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105962/selection/546883b9441c5fb3a054379dab9c65355fde2da3d83c5d3f7f0727159514b942" :answer/id #uuid "aa0838e4-4b65-5cd3-9e16-3e3664ea7433" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105962/selection/c457855895bc1067a6194394000ebd060f4468538e77f0a1b68c4b2c254c1515" :answer/id #uuid "56c6af0c-9d43-5e7f-bed0-67f4f17f5a9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,0,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105962/selection/d95df56a481c9d8bede0576d7abae0a731cd2f3c7a2cb4596d909e521e910b9b" :answer/id #uuid "c0099fbf-e63f-5c4a-9e51-391aa48552c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,0,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105962/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "348feb3f-872e-5d93-8894-a7826f49b08e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105962/selection/613f439dc6324c3c1f9ff32eea8f2121282ac7a544cf9d808b85c34a9e6b0b25" :answer-field/choices ["q-105962/selection/eee5a3a8e12930dd100249b1242ad7e1794b48a6f0e204e718f698c7792ed534" "q-105962/selection/613f439dc6324c3c1f9ff32eea8f2121282ac7a544cf9d808b85c34a9e6b0b25" "q-105962/selection/546883b9441c5fb3a054379dab9c65355fde2da3d83c5d3f7f0727159514b942" "q-105962/selection/c457855895bc1067a6194394000ebd060f4468538e77f0a1b68c4b2c254c1515" "q-105962/selection/d95df56a481c9d8bede0576d7abae0a731cd2f3c7a2cb4596d909e521e910b9b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105962" :question/id #uuid "af5d832d-bffb-56c4-8e12-6440a08b81a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-105962" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x,0,yz⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=y-{x}^{2}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨z,0,0⟩,\\,∇f=⟨-2x,1,0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(0,2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2x & 1 & 0 \\\\ x & 0 & yz\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1(yz)-0(0)]i-[-2x(yz)-0(x)]j+[-2x(0)-1(x)]k \\\\  & =yz\\,i+2xyz\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =⟨yz,2xyz,-x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(y-{x}^{2})⟨z,0,0⟩+⟨yz,2xyz,-x⟩ \\\\  & =⟨z(y-{x}^{2}),0,0⟩+⟨yz,2xyz,-x⟩ \\\\  & =⟨z(2y-{x}^{2}),2xyz,-x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(0,2,-1) & =⟨(-1)(2(2)-(0)^{2}),2(0)(2)(-1),-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105962/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105962"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131473/selection/141aa21a96bc88077930953a71ee1ab01f3164e0acb69ff5ea46f572efd62afe" :answer/id #uuid "0c036cb5-5d41-57cf-8a56-454bb9f35983" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,-2,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131473/selection/f5fcee3e358d7581ead658f119e2dfb88247586f43f33b5053edd11e8d09305f" :answer/id #uuid "ec94f6ad-0a1a-53f5-894e-cd5befc43526" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131473/selection/57c41db8113644e55c0d66c068037ca6c28229c674e0db7422a42993d9b63232" :answer/id #uuid "1f51a641-718d-5401-9491-34d2244c4bf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,-1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131473/selection/a3fa112e58e5acfb3df0b282ebd12da75237226371246e6c0123ecb12db429b9" :answer/id #uuid "8d996f81-30fe-5e69-8245-11f5e55f2d0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131473/selection/65decf87ef748f1cb7530580a3b4724c36517c1ff6ede8066038da77b3e9ec33" :answer/id #uuid "49b4e40f-b00b-5817-938a-be697a9f9f34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131473/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c4e64be-4dca-54cc-8b48-c32c25eeacab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131473/selection/a3fa112e58e5acfb3df0b282ebd12da75237226371246e6c0123ecb12db429b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-131473/selection/141aa21a96bc88077930953a71ee1ab01f3164e0acb69ff5ea46f572efd62afe" "q-131473/selection/f5fcee3e358d7581ead658f119e2dfb88247586f43f33b5053edd11e8d09305f" "q-131473/selection/57c41db8113644e55c0d66c068037ca6c28229c674e0db7422a42993d9b63232" "q-131473/selection/a3fa112e58e5acfb3df0b282ebd12da75237226371246e6c0123ecb12db429b9" "q-131473/selection/65decf87ef748f1cb7530580a3b4724c36517c1ff6ede8066038da77b3e9ec33"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131473" :question/id #uuid "dd04d4a1-06a3-54bf-b4fa-64c9c940f43b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131473" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,y,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=xyz.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩,\\,∇f=⟨yz,xz,xy⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(1,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ yz & xz & xy \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡z & y & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[(xz)(0)-(y)(xy)]i-[(yz)(0)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)(xy)]j+[(yz)(y)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)(xz)]k \\\\  & =-x{y}^{2}\\,i+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,j+(z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =xyz⟨0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩+⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-xyz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩+⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},-xyz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},-xy(z\\operatorname{sin}⁡z-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z),z({y}^{2}-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(1,1,0) & =⟨-1,-(0\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131473/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131473"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131472/selection/12a00006ba1febf77872115d07283f6531dceabf7dbb679442130a87064d7cbd" :answer/id #uuid "f09a77bb-2cf3-55f3-b76c-f4d7c5a179b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,0,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131472/selection/8c67a57ee0ff885d6f63260c439282247d859fa48cc34c03d77a53a1d60b5697" :answer/id #uuid "0c458aff-f913-55aa-84ca-51b75156d635" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,-4,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131472/selection/93291471a5a2a4104c09597e3851ddc449e7059057de367e274d4d6b0042a417" :answer/id #uuid "8edb551c-2d4c-554e-8dc4-cf0400b2b8cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,0,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131472/selection/576b0b309b18a7a9d234af8da171802460eb78fe42fff6096771c76de66094e8" :answer/id #uuid "8a18d430-e032-5465-a03a-a010a788d7c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,-4,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131472/selection/d7cf8bc3a32f526a2c13fc96bee0fec39986d3777aa9944f9914062fbeb666c3" :answer/id #uuid "406ccd77-3980-59a5-8576-2c4f848f625e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨6,3,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131472/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "177a3fba-eb36-5fed-ad62-66ad84cebe74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131472/selection/93291471a5a2a4104c09597e3851ddc449e7059057de367e274d4d6b0042a417" :answer-field/choices ["q-131472/selection/12a00006ba1febf77872115d07283f6531dceabf7dbb679442130a87064d7cbd" "q-131472/selection/8c67a57ee0ff885d6f63260c439282247d859fa48cc34c03d77a53a1d60b5697" "q-131472/selection/93291471a5a2a4104c09597e3851ddc449e7059057de367e274d4d6b0042a417" "q-131472/selection/576b0b309b18a7a9d234af8da171802460eb78fe42fff6096771c76de66094e8" "q-131472/selection/d7cf8bc3a32f526a2c13fc96bee0fec39986d3777aa9944f9914062fbeb666c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131472" :question/id #uuid "4c83f641-aa51-5d02-9db8-4bfd683b6333" :question/math-academy-id "q-131472" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨0,x,2\\sqrt{y}⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=y{z}^{2}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}},0,1⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,{z}^{2},2yz⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(0,4,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & {z}^{2} & 2yz \\\\ 0 & x & 2\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[({z}^{2})(2\\sqrt{y})-(x)(2yz)]i-[(0)(2\\sqrt{y})-(0)(2yz)]j+[(0)(x)-(0)({z}^{2})]k \\\\  & =(2{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-2xyz)\\,i+0\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =⟨2{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-2xyz,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(y{z}^{2})⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}},0,1⟩+⟨2{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-2xyz,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y},0,y{z}^{2}⟩+⟨2{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-2xyz,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{z}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-2xyz,0,y{z}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)(0,4,1)=⟨6,0,4⟩.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131472/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131472"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105960/selection/9ed6025f01c9de3cab62a8ef58ea0d8eb1f4bca73474a4d4e5a038ba71169182" :answer/id #uuid "35458e74-26df-5fdd-ad09-56f7448b05c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,-1,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105960/selection/0ebad4434b3314665251f0033302015b811732b78ea2fdc9bd5be1f0703fe87e" :answer/id #uuid "37f3d8e4-db0c-5b7f-9fb1-aa41f6b51dfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,-3,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105960/selection/5620dbfb46ad49652977b00e9d384f57f18bb215338e9bc55041cfcce912cc12" :answer/id #uuid "4eb95285-8f0e-50b8-af16-e46f9ff33446" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-4,-2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105960/selection/eddc486db9f2fcd279606ef706f3affc97d9a509e381a7376e62e941150bd858" :answer/id #uuid "e71cb85e-a4af-578f-93d4-c63f9fb31b8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,2,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105960/selection/4480af35eb37fcd4a07897de0b3817c47e2439d63ef22c8da2b7df6842b5614b" :answer/id #uuid "57daca68-ee0c-53d9-811a-98d736cdf6d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,0,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105960/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c913ebb-c3cc-525f-98e7-b8a256daed0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105960/selection/0ebad4434b3314665251f0033302015b811732b78ea2fdc9bd5be1f0703fe87e" :answer-field/choices ["q-105960/selection/9ed6025f01c9de3cab62a8ef58ea0d8eb1f4bca73474a4d4e5a038ba71169182" "q-105960/selection/0ebad4434b3314665251f0033302015b811732b78ea2fdc9bd5be1f0703fe87e" "q-105960/selection/5620dbfb46ad49652977b00e9d384f57f18bb215338e9bc55041cfcce912cc12" "q-105960/selection/eddc486db9f2fcd279606ef706f3affc97d9a509e381a7376e62e941150bd858" "q-105960/selection/4480af35eb37fcd4a07897de0b3817c47e2439d63ef22c8da2b7df6842b5614b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105960" :question/id #uuid "f8e48e04-f390-56ea-9c62-53bc38b6727e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105960" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,0,z⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{x}{y}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,0,-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x⟩,\\,∇f=⟨\\frac{1}{y},-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}},0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(1,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} & 0 \\\\ y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & 0 & z\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}(z)-0(0)]i-[\\frac{1}{y}(z)-0(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)]j+[\\frac{1}{y}(0)-(-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}})(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)]k \\\\  & =-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{z}{y}\\,j+\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{y}⟨0,0,-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x⟩+⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,-\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩+⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{xz}{{y}^{2}},-\\frac{z}{y},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(1,1,3) & =⟨-\\frac{1(3)}{(1)^{2}},-\\frac{3}{1},0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105960/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105960"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105894/selection/13cb6c5da950ef5f936873ab2bc4a015f5f8125ec00c5e42ae48e1e9ebc8ca6e" :answer/id #uuid "4541c2a3-78c5-5c95-b7d8-f29d88f7f288" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,-1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105894/selection/104c8589f3a5454fe2b1c57b9b2a385499976b322c976dc2be54fb81b45fb84f" :answer/id #uuid "2c4d57e2-d89e-546a-8c45-0250391dbddd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,0,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105894/selection/eca61f1b84786d16ad626af7ba601bb554c91c7a8e27048a60a489599617710e" :answer/id #uuid "bb9c49e3-b3d7-574f-829a-595add9678c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,0,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105894/selection/3d9f2a089ca5602ee53bd725b6fa9f4fa5f32a4221baeb0fb2e76fbaa5a84646" :answer/id #uuid "f35cbb04-9eeb-53ae-95c8-7a5f97e679b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,0,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105894/selection/a51de418aa7407d3dc84d3aeaedca3fbdbf926ab36a8821b9f6ce35705195712" :answer/id #uuid "f812b48e-8516-5c0b-b2e0-ae4951cf97bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-1,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105894/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2453c30-2ebc-5720-8567-5235873a1248" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105894/selection/a51de418aa7407d3dc84d3aeaedca3fbdbf926ab36a8821b9f6ce35705195712" :answer-field/choices ["q-105894/selection/13cb6c5da950ef5f936873ab2bc4a015f5f8125ec00c5e42ae48e1e9ebc8ca6e" "q-105894/selection/104c8589f3a5454fe2b1c57b9b2a385499976b322c976dc2be54fb81b45fb84f" "q-105894/selection/eca61f1b84786d16ad626af7ba601bb554c91c7a8e27048a60a489599617710e" "q-105894/selection/3d9f2a089ca5602ee53bd725b6fa9f4fa5f32a4221baeb0fb2e76fbaa5a84646" "q-105894/selection/a51de418aa7407d3dc84d3aeaedca3fbdbf926ab36a8821b9f6ce35705195712"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105894" :question/id #uuid "029ad381-66bf-5214-8d8c-c8e093cae3d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-105894" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),y,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=1+{z}^{2}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z),0⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,0,2z⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(\\pi ,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2z \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z) & y & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(0)-2z(y)]i-[0(0)-2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)]j+[0(y)-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)]k \\\\  & =-2yz\\,i+2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z)j+0\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(1+{z}^{2})⟨0,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z),0⟩+⟨-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,(1+{z}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z),0⟩+⟨-2yz,2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2yz,(1+{z}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+z)+2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(\\pi ,1,0) & =⟨-2(1)(0),(1+(0)^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi +0)+2(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi +0),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105894/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8745"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\nabla\\times(3\\mathbf{F} + \\mathbf{G})$ at the point $(-1,1,0)$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G,$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = 3x\\,\\mathbf{i} + y^2z\\,\\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}, \\quad (\\nabla\\times\\mathbf{G})(x,y,z) = 3y^2\\,\\mathbf{i} + 4z\\,\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F$\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\times \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =∇\\times (3F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3x & {y}^{2}z & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x)]k \\\\  & =(0-{y}^{2})i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3[-{y}^{2}\\,i]+[3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k] \\\\  & =-3{y}^{2}\\,i+3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =(3{y}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =4z\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,1,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(-1,1,0) & =4(0)\\,j+k=k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8931"] :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z) =  \\langle 0, y-z, x-y\\rangle$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z) = x+y.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times \\mathbf F = \\langle 0,\\,-1,\\,0\\rangle, \n\\quad\n\\nabla f = \\langle 1,\\, 1,\\, 0\\rangle,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F)$ at the point $(-1,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F) = f \\nabla \\times \\mathbf {F}+   \\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & y-z & x-y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (y-z)]\\,i-[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (0)]\\,j+[1\\cdot (y-z)-1\\cdot (0)]\\,k \\\\  & =(x-y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j+(y-z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x+y)⟨0,-1,0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-(x+y),0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,-2x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(-1,1,3) & =⟨(-1)-1,\\,-2(-1),\\,1-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
